.TH XD\-LOCK 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-lock \- Lock Computer and screen savers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-lock
.YS
.SY xd\-lock
.B \-\-saver
.RI [ id ]
.RB [ \-\-lock | \-\-no\-lock ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without options,
.B xd\-lock
locks the computer as Windows 2000 did: the screen says
\(lqComputer Locked\(rq, and Ctrl+Alt+Delete opens Unlock Computer, which
checks the user's password with PAM.
After the screen saver's usual wait, a locked computer runs the screen
saver.
Win+L runs it.
.PP
It locks with the ext-session-lock protocol: the compositor shows nothing
else until it unlocks, and keeps the screen locked if it crashes
.RB ( xd\-compositor (1)
then starts it again).
When the display manager's greeter lets the user back in after Switch
User, logind tells it to unlock, so the password isn't asked twice; and
logind's Lock
.RB ( "loginctl lock\-session" )
turns a running screen saver into a locked screen.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-saver ,
it runs a screen saver until the mouse moves or a key is pressed.
.BR xd\-shell (1)
runs it after the Wait set in Display Properties.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-saver " [\fIid\fR]"
Run the screen saver
.IR id ,
or the one chosen in Display Properties:
.BR flowerbox " (3D Flower Box), " maze " (3D Maze), "
.BR pipes " (3D Pipes), " text3d " (3D Text), " beziers ,
.BR blank " (Blank Screen), " flying " (Flying Penguins), "
.BR marquee " (Marquee Display), " mystify " (Mystify Your Mind) or "
.B starfield
(Starfield Simulation).
.TP
.B \-\-lock
With
.BR \-\-saver ,
lock when the saver ends, asking for the password.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-lock
With
.BR \-\-saver ,
don't lock.
Without either, the saver's Password protected setting decides.
.TP
.BI \-\-style " style"
.TQ
.BI \-\-scheme " file"
The visual style and colour scheme instead of those in
.IR desktop.ini .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/desktop.ini
The screen saver, its Wait and Password protected, and each saver's
settings
.RB ( [ScreenSaver] ", " [ScreenSaver.*] ).
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/xeondesktop
The PAM service the password is checked with; without it,
.IR login 's.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-desk (1),
.BR xd\-shell (1),
.BR loginctl (1)
